#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# sinc

#% text
# `sinc(x)` gives sin(x)/x, with `sinc(0)` = 1.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `sinc` is even; exact values follow those of `sin`.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
sinc(0)
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
sinc(pi/2)
#% output
#= 2/pi

#% cell
sinc(0.3)
#% output
#= 0.9850673555377986

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
sinc(-x)
#% output
#= sinc(x)

#% cell
sinc([pi, 2*pi, 1.5])
#% output
#= [0, 0, 0.6649966577360362]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `sin`, `sinh`
